---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../site.config';

const { controllerIdentity, controllerContact } = site.legal;
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How this website handles personal data under the UK GDPR and the Data Protection Act 2018."
>
  <p>
    This policy explains how personal data is handled when you visit this website, in line with the UK
    General Data Protection Regulation (UK GDPR) and the Data Protection Act 2018.
  </p>

  <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
  <p>
    The data controller for this website is {controllerIdentity}.
    You can contact the controller at {controllerContact}.
  </p>

  <h2>What this website does not do</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>It does not set cookies.</li>
    <li>It does not use analytics, tracking pixels, advertising tools or any other tracking.</li>
    <li>It has no forms, accounts, comments or newsletter sign-up.</li>
    <li>
      It loads nothing from other websites while you browse: its fonts and images are served from this
      website.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>The website itself therefore does not collect or store any personal data about you.</p>

  <h2>Hosting and server logs</h2>
  <p>
    This website is hosted by Vercel Inc. (see the <a href="/legal/">Legal notice</a>). To deliver each
    page, Vercel's servers necessarily receive your IP address and basic technical details of the request,
    such as the page requested, the time of the request and the type of browser. Vercel processes this
    data, including in server logs, as a processor acting on behalf of the controller, to deliver the
    website and to keep it secure.
  </p>
  <p>
    The lawful basis for this processing is legitimate interests (<span class="nowrap">Article 6(1)(f)</span> UK GDPR): showing you
    the website you asked for and protecting it against misuse.
  </p>
  <p>
    Vercel Inc. is based in the United States, so this data may be processed outside the UK. Vercel's
    Data Processing Addendum provides for such transfers using the UK International Data Transfer
    Addendum to the EU Standard Contractual Clauses.
  </p>
  <p>Server logs are kept for [PLACEHOLDER: server log retention period under the Vercel plan in use].</p>

  <h2>Links to Etsy and Gelato</h2>
  <p>
    Original works are sold on Etsy and prints are ordered through Gelato. When you follow a link to
    either, you leave this website. Etsy and Gelato are independent third parties with their own privacy
    and cookie policies, which apply to anything you do on their websites.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>Under the UK GDPR you have the right to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>be informed about how your personal data is used;</li>
    <li>access your personal data;</li>
    <li>have inaccurate personal data corrected;</li>
    <li>have your personal data erased;</li>
    <li>restrict how your personal data is used;</li>
    <li>object to the use of your personal data;</li>
    <li>data portability, where it applies.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    To exercise any of these rights, contact the controller at {controllerContact}. Because the website
    itself holds no personal data, a request can only concern the server logs processed by Vercel.
  </p>

  <h2>Complaints</h2>
  <p>
    You can raise a concern about how your personal data has been handled with the controller, using
    the contact details above.
  </p>
  <p>
    You also have the right to complain to the Information Commissioner's Office (ICO), the UK
    regulator for data protection, online at <a href="https://ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint/">ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint</a> or by telephone on 0303 123 1113.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
